---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, PHONE_DISPLAY, mailtoHref, telHref } from '@/lib/contact';

const title = 'Terms of Service';
const description =
  'Terms governing use of NutaSolutions websites and NutaPOS, including accounts, Customer Content, and Ghana governing law.';
const lastUpdated = 'September 10, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-24 pt-32 md:px-6 md:pt-36">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    <div class="mt-10 max-w-none space-y-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <p>
        These Terms of Service (“Terms”) form a binding agreement between you and NutaSolutions (“NutaSolutions,” “we,”
        “us,” or “our”) governing access to and use of our websites, NutaPOS, and related services (the “Services”).
      </p>
      <p>
        By accessing the Services, creating an account, or clicking to accept these Terms, you agree to them. If you use
        the Services on behalf of a business, you represent that you have authority to bind that business, and “you”
        includes that business.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">1. The Services</h2>
      <p>
        NutaPOS is a cloud point-of-sale and business management platform for sales, inventory, bookkeeping, staff
        access, audits, and related operations. Features may evolve over time. Marketing materials describe intended
        capabilities; the Services available to your account are those enabled for your plan and configuration.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">2. Accounts and eligibility</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>You must provide accurate signup and business information and keep it up to date.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for safeguarding credentials and for activity under your account and user seats.</li>
        <li>Notify us promptly of unauthorised access or suspected compromise.</li>
        <li>
          You must be able to form a binding contract under applicable law (typically 18 years or older, or acting
          through a duly authorised representative).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">3. Plans, fees, and taxes</h2>
      <p>
        We offer plan tiers (such as Starter, Growth, and Enterprise) that may begin with a free start, sales-led
        onboarding, or custom pricing. Fees, billing cadence, and included features are as agreed in an order form,
        invoice, or written quote, or as displayed at signup when self-serve pricing is available.
      </p>
      <p>
        Unless stated otherwise, fees are quoted in Ghanaian cedi (GHS) or another currency we specify, and are
        exclusive of applicable taxes (including VAT). You are responsible for taxes arising from your purchase, except
        taxes based on our net income. Late or failed payment may result in suspension after reasonable notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not currently process card payments on the marketing website. When payment providers are introduced, their
        terms and our billing practices will apply as disclosed at checkout or in your order.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">4. Licence and acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to these Terms, we grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right to access and
        use the Services for your internal business operations during your subscription.
      </p>
      <p>You must not:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
        <li>Use the Services for unlawful purposes or to process illegal goods or transactions</li>
        <li>Probe, scan, or disrupt the Services, or attempt to bypass security or access controls</li>
        <li>Reverse engineer the software except to the extent such restriction is prohibited by law</li>
        <li>Resell, sublicense, or provide the Services to third parties as a competing offering without our consent</li>
        <li>Scrape or harvest data from the Services in a way that harms performance or violates others’ rights</li>
        <li>Upload malware or content that infringes intellectual property or privacy rights</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">5. Customer Content</h2>
      <p>
        “Customer Content” means data you and your authorised users submit to or generate in NutaPOS, including sales
        and inventory records, bookkeeping data, staff profiles, audit information, and any end-customer information
        captured in your operations.
      </p>
      <p>
        You retain ownership of Customer Content. You grant NutaSolutions a worldwide licence to host, store, process,
        transmit, and display Customer Content solely as needed to provide, secure, and improve the Services and as
        otherwise directed by you.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the legality of Customer Content and for providing any required notices and obtaining
        any required consents from your staff, end customers, and other data subjects under the Data Protection Act,
        2012 (Act 843) and other applicable laws.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">6. Processing of Customer Content</h2>
      <p>
        For Customer Content, you are the data controller and NutaSolutions is a data processor. We will process
        Customer Content only to provide the Services, in accordance with these Terms and your documented instructions
        (including configuration and use of the product), and applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will maintain appropriate confidentiality and security measures, and may engage subprocessors (such as cloud
        hosting providers) to support delivery of the Services. We remain responsible for subprocessors’ performance
        insofar as they process Customer Content on our behalf.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">7. Availability and support</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the Services available and reliable using commercially reasonable efforts. Scheduled maintenance,
        updates, or events beyond our reasonable control may cause interruptions. Unless a separate service level
        agreement says otherwise, we do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Support is available through
        <a href={mailtoHref('Support request')} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
        and
        <a href={telHref()} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a>,
        subject to your plan.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        NutaSolutions and its licensors own all rights in the Services, software, documentation, branding, and related
        intellectual property. These Terms do not transfer ownership to you. Feedback you provide may be used by us
        without obligation to you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">9. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The Services may link to or integrate with third-party products. Those products are governed by their own terms
        and privacy policies. We are not responsible for third-party services we do not control.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">10. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by Ghana law, the Services are provided “as is” and “as available,” without
        warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that
        the Services will meet all of your business requirements or that data will never be lost; you should maintain
        appropriate backups and internal controls for your operations.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">11. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, NutaSolutions will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special,
        consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, goodwill, or data, arising from or related to
        the Services or these Terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our aggregate liability for all claims relating to the Services in any twelve-month period will not exceed the
        amounts you paid to NutaSolutions for the Services in that period (or, if you are on a free plan with no fees
        paid, GHS 500). Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot be limited under Ghana law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">12. Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        You will defend and indemnify NutaSolutions against claims, losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal
        fees) arising from Customer Content, your misuse of the Services, your violation of these Terms, or your
        violation of third-party rights or applicable law in connection with your business use of NutaPOS.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">13. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        You may stop using the Services at any time. We may suspend or terminate access if you materially breach these
        Terms, fail to pay fees when due, create risk to the Services or others, or if we are required to do so by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        Upon termination, your licence ends. We will make Customer Content available for export for a reasonable period
        (typically up to 30 days) upon written request, after which we may delete it from active systems in accordance
        with our Privacy Policy, subject to legal retention requirements and backup cycles.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Ghana. Courts located in Ghana have exclusive
        jurisdiction over disputes arising from these Terms or the Services, without prejudice to any non-waivable
        consumer or statutory rights that may apply.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">15. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date will change when we do. Material changes
        may be communicated by email or in-product notice. Continued use after the effective date constitutes
        acceptance of the updated Terms where permitted by law. If you do not agree, you must stop using the Services.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">16. General</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy and any order form or quote we both accept, are the entire
        agreement regarding the Services and supersede prior conflicting discussions on the same subject. If a
        provision is unenforceable, the remainder stays in effect. You may not assign these Terms without our consent;
        we may assign them in connection with a corporate reorganisation or sale of assets. Failure to enforce a
        provision is not a waiver.
      </p>

      <h2 class="!mt-10 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-surface-900">17. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        NutaSolutions<br />
        Email:
        <a href={mailtoHref('Terms inquiry')} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a><br />
        Phone:
        <a href={telHref()} class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700">{PHONE_DISPLAY}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
